From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad House <brad-house@example.net>
Date: Mon, 1 Jun 2026 07:12:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] sonic-mgmt-common: port to libyang3 (#157)

Port to libyang3 while maintaining compatibility for libyang1.

An abstraction layer has been added to aid in the compatibility.  That said, in the long term libyang1 support should be removed once compatibility is no longer needed.

Signed-off-by: Brad House <brad-house@example.net>
(cherry picked from commit cdb612efcf6835f8dc3f004e214440ed8b744644)

[202511 backport] Taken unchanged except azure-pipelines.yml, whose hunk
was written against master's trixie paths: the same change (install
libyang3 and libyang-dev 3 instead of libyang 1.0.73) on 202511's
bookworm paths.
---
 azure-pipelines.yml             |    3 +-
 cvl/cvl.go                      |   27 +-
 cvl/cvl_api.go                  |   17 +-
 cvl/cvl_error_test.go           |   18 +-
 cvl/cvl_semantics.go            |    9 +-
 cvl/cvl_syntax.go               |   77 +-
 cvl/cvl_test.go                 |   18 +-
 cvl/cvl_when_test.go            |   12 +-
